# Every pattern here is anchored with a leading slash, and that is not tidiness.
#
# `.vercelignore` follows .gitignore matching, where a pattern without a slash
# matches a directory of that name at ANY depth. `tools/` was meant to keep the
# mutation scripts out of the build. It also matched `app/tools/` — the route
# that shows both system prompts verbatim — so that page was never uploaded, and
# the deployed nav linked to a 404 while every local check passed. Nothing in
# this repository could have caught it, because the file was correct about the
# directory it was named for.
#
# tests/deployment.test.ts now fails if any pattern here would swallow a route.

# The Playwright runner never ships. It is a separate package with its own
# manifest, so Vercel's `npm install` at the project root cannot pull Chromium
# into a build that will never launch one. Excluding the directory outright is
# the second line of defence: nothing to upload, nothing to trace, nothing to
# accidentally import from an app file.
/runner/

# Recording and verification are for a developer machine and CI, not the
# serverless build.
/record-runs.sh
/verify-deployment.sh
/tests/
/tools/
